      "notes": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:uuid:d82ae537-e6f1-5379-8e62-e9a6b295a170",
          "@type": "Note",
          "content": "CONTRACTOR TO VERIFY ALL NOTES AND DIMENSIONS AND REPORT ANY DISCREPANCIES TO DESIGNER PRIOR TO CONSTRUCTION.\nWRITTEN DIMENSIONS TAKE PRECEDENCE OVER SCALED DIMENSIONS.\nALL COMPONENTS OF DWGS TO COMPLY WITH CURRENT VANCOUVER BUILDING BYLAW.",
          "bbox": [
            2311,
            336,
            2486,
            471
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:uuid:1f80cd15-85a2-509c-8174-1712e3c61601",
          "@type": "Note",
          "content": "SUITE WALL & CEILING ASSEMBLY\nWALL ASSEMBLY - W 6d: Fire Resistance Rating 1 hr, Sound Transmission Class (STC) 55. 2 layers 1/2\" Type 'X' gypsum board; 2x4 wood studs spaced 16\" o.c.; R-14 sound batt insulation; resilient metal channels @ 16\" o.c.; 2 layers 1/2\" Type 'X' gypsum board.\nFLOOR/CEILING ASSEMBLY - F 15i: Fire Resistance Rating 1 hr, Sound Transmission Class (STC) 61. Finished floor on 1 1/2\" concrete topping; 5/8\" T&G plywood subfloor; wood joists spaced not more than 24\" o.c.; R-28 sound batt insulation; resilient metal channels @ 16\" o.c.; 2 layers 1/2\" Type 'X' gypsum board.",
          "bbox": [
            984,
            464,
            1268,
            705
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:uuid:ab35a774-3b87-554f-8461-b1523e65c7cd",
          "@type": "Note",
          "content": "ALL SOFFITS LESS THAN 3.94 FT FROM PROPERTY LINE TO BE NON VENTED SOLID MATERIAL CONSTRUCTION.",
          "bbox": [
            964,
            433,
            1240,
            453
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:uuid:9152d15b-bb01-55a8-9688-7b07bfe98b2c",
          "@type": "Note",
          "content": "CEA VERIFICATION GUIDELINES\n1.1 ABOVE GRADE WALLS: ON PLAN WALL INSULATION MEETS OR EXCEEDS R22 EFFECTIVE AND BUILDER PROVIDED R22 GUIDE\n1.2 ATTIC AND FLAT CEILING: ON PLAN ATTIC (R50) AND FLAT CEILING (R28) INSULATION MEETS OR EXCEEDS REQ. NOM. R VALUES\n1.3 FOUNDATION WALLS AND UNDER SLAB: ON PLAN WALL INSULATION MEETS OR EXCEEDS R22 EFFECTIVE, UNDER SLAB MEETS OR EXCEEDS R12 NOMINAL\n1.4 EXPOSED FLOORS: ON PLAN WALL INSULATION MEETS OR EXCEEDS R28 NOMINAL\n1.5 HEADERS: ON PLAN WALL INSULATION MEETS OR EXCEEDS R22 EFFECTIVE\n1.6 CONTINUOUS INSULATION: INSULATION ON PLAN IS CONTINUOUS INCLUDING DUCTS OUTSIDE THE ENVELOPE\n1.7 AIR BARRIER: AIR BARRIER IS PLANNED TO BE CONTINUOUS\n2.1 WINDOWS: SPECIFIED WINDOWS AND GLASS DOORS MEET USI 1.4 (R4.06) OR LOWER\n2.2 SKYLIGHTS: SPECIFIED SKYLIGHTS ON PLANS ARE USI 2.4 (OR LOWER)\nCEA TO INFORM THAT HRV WITH 65% OR BETTER SENSIBLE HEAT RECOVERY / IN CONDITIONED SPACE / ACCEPTABLE FOR FILTER MAINTENANCE INDICATED\n3.2 FURNACE/BOILER: CEA TO INFORM MINIMUM 92% EFFICIENT AFUE, NO SIDE\n3.3 HOT WATER TANK OR ON DEMAND: CEA TO INFORM THAT DOMESTIC HOT WATER HEATER MUST BE 78% OR GREATER EFFICIENCY OR AT INDIRECT SOURCE. ELECTRIC TANK TO BE WRAPPED RSI 1.75 (R10)\n3.4 HOT WATER PIPE: INFORM THAT THE FIRST 3m FROM AND THE LAST 1m TO ALL HOT WATER SHALL HAVE PIPE INSULATION WITH AN RSI OF 0.35 (R2)\n3.5 RECIRCULATING SYSTEM: CEA TO INFORM THE ENTIRE PIPE SYSTEM MUST BE WRAPPED WITH PIPE INSULATION WITH RSI OF 0.35 (R2.84)",
          "bbox": [
            1281,
            349,
            1574,
            971
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:uuid:6b886f8b-c43a-559a-9136-83574c5b0a9a",
          "@type": "Note",
          "content": "TYPICAL CRAWL SPACE MAXIMUM CLEAR HEIGHT 3'-11\" VENTED 1 SQFT PER 500 SQFT FLR. AREA MINIMUM 2 VENTS.",
          "bbox": [
            982,
            1049,
            1118,
            1102
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:uuid:ba89ce4d-5126-5c75-8b3d-64a9a85072c8",
          "@type": "Note",
          "content": "SCUPPER OVERFLOWS TO BE PROVIDED AT ALL BALCONIES ENCLOSED WITH PARAPET WALLS.\nINTERIOR GUARDRAILS TO 36\" HIGH. EXTERIOR GUARDRAILS TO 42\" HIGH.\nHANDRAILS ON BOTH SIDES OF STAIRS GREATER THAN 44\" WIDE.\nALL INTERIOR FRAMING DIMENSIONS ARE TO CENTERLINE OF STUDS UNLESS NOTED OTHERWISE.\nSECURITY BLOCKING TO BE PROVIDED AT ALL EXTERIOR DOORS.\nBUILDING TO BE SPRINKLERED TO NFPA 13D.\nSAFETY GLASS TO BE USED WITHIN 3'-0\" OF DOOR ENTRY LOCKS, AT ENTRANCE DOORS AND SIDELIGHTS, NEAR BATHTUBS AND JACUZZIS.\nWATERPROOF BACKING MATERIAL TO BE PROVIDED AROUND BATHTUBS AND SHOWERS.\nCOMBUSTION AIR TO BE SUPPLIED AT ALL SOLID FUEL BURNING APPLIANCES AT OR NEAR THE APPLIANCES.",
          "bbox": [
            316,
            1197,
            874,
            1363
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
